WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.260
Hi, I'm Boba!

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:05.815
FastH3 is a distilled MiniMax H3, a model that makes video

00:00:05.815 --> 00:00:07.108
with its own audio.

00:00:07.108 --> 00:00:10.017
Here are the two levers that speed it up.

00:00:11.475 --> 00:00:15.524
Call the transformer 4 times instead of 49, by distilling it, and

00:00:15.524 --> 00:00:20.247
make each call cheaper, by letting only about one attention tile in ten through.

00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:23.910
Training starts from prompts alone.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.952
No video, real or synthetic, is ever loaded.

00:00:26.952 --> 00:00:28.474
That's what Data-Free means.

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:33.169
The student, running sparse attention, generates its own sample from pure noise,

00:00:33.169 --> 00:00:34.594
in four fixed steps.

00:00:35.014 --> 00:00:38.897
A frozen dense teacher and a trainable critic, both from the same

00:00:38.897 --> 00:00:42.134
H3 weights, score it at a randomly sampled noise level.

00:00:42.554 --> 00:00:45.929
Their scores pull the student's outputs toward the teacher's distribution.

00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:49.304
The critic trains five times as often, to keep up.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.590
Base H3 attends densely.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:58.026
Inside each call, VSA cuts the video into 3D tiles of sixty-four tokens.

00:00:58.446 --> 00:01:00.981
A cheap pooled pass scores every tile.

00:01:00.981 --> 00:01:05.690
At ninety percent sparsity, only about one tile in ten gets exact attention.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.790
The losing tiles aren't dropped.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.821
A trained gate, about one point nine three billion new parameters, blends

00:01:11.821 --> 00:01:13.500
a pooled summary back in.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:19.564
On a fifteen-second clip, distillation alone gives seven point four three times.

00:01:19.564 --> 00:01:24.455
Sparsity multiplies that by one point nine three, for fourteen point three eight.

00:01:25.975 --> 00:01:28.605
Fewer calls and cheaper calls are separate levers.

00:01:28.605 --> 00:01:32.221
They multiply, and the longer the clip, the more sparsity pays.

00:01:34.275 --> 00:01:38.691
To recap: four calls instead of forty-nine, trained from prompts alone, one

00:01:38.691 --> 00:01:40.532
tile in ten attended exactly.

00:01:40.952 --> 00:01:43.024
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:43.024 --> 00:01:43.615
I'm Boba.

00:01:43.615 --> 00:01:43.911
Bye!
